{"id":"word:hebrew:H5175","type":"word","title":"נָחָשׁ","subtitle":"H5175 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a snake (from its hiss)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נָחָשׁ (H5175) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 31 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נָחָשׁ (nâchâsh) means a snake (from its hiss) First listed occurrence: 2Kgs 18 4."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נָחָשׁ","transliteration":"nâchâsh","pronunciation":"naw-khawsh'","strong":"H5175","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5175","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["הַ/נָּחָ֖שׁ","הַ/נָּחָ֑שׁ","נָחָ֣שׁ","נְחַ֨שׁ","הַ/נָּחָֽשׁ"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",10],["HTd/Ncmsa",9],["HNcmsc",3],["HR/Ncmsa",3],["HRd/Ncmsa",2],["HC/Td/Ncmsa",1],["HC/Ncmsa",1],["HNcmpa",1],["HTd/Ncmpa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a snake (from its hiss)","usage":"serpent.","full":"H5175. nachash I. נָחָשׁ noun masculine Gen 3:1 serpent (Late Hebrew id.; Arabic serpent, viper (Lane 406anything hunted ) is compare by Lag M, i, 230 ; BN 50, 188 Ba Es 48 , but improbable; Arabic see below [ נָחַשׁ below; on formation compare Lag BN 50 ); — absolute ׳נ Amos 5:19 +; construct נְחַשׁ Num 21:9 2 t.; plural נְחָשִׁים 21:6 ; Jer 8:17 ; &#8212; 1 serpent: a. as biting , Amos 5:19 ; Eccl 10:8 , in spite of charm ( לַחַשׁ ) 10:11 [compare Ecculs 12:13 ], Jer 8:17 (+ צִפְעֹנִים ; figurative of enemies); so הַשְׁרָפִים הַנְּחָשִׁים Num 21:6 (deadly; J E; compare Jacob Arab. Dicht. iv. 10 ff. ), and singular 21:9 , also (collective) 21:7 compare ׳נ שָׂרָף Deut 8:15 (+ עַקְרָב ); ׳נ figurative of oppressor, מְעוֺפֵף שָׂרָף וּפִרְיוֺ צֶפַע יֵצֵא נָחָשׁ מִשֹּׁרֶשׁ Isa 14:29 ; figurative of Dan Gen 49:17 (poem in J; || שְׁפִיפֹן ); נ ׳הֲמַת Psa 58:5 (simile of perniciousness of ungodly), compare ׳נ 140:4 ; simile of effect of wine Proverbs 22:32 (|| צִפִעֹנִי ). b. rod becomes ׳נ Exod 4:3 (J), compare 7:15 (E); נ דֶּרֶךְ צוּר ׳עֲלֵי Prov 30:19 . c. ׳נ (apparently) as hissing Jer 46:22 (in simile, compare Gie); as eating dust Isa 65:25 compare Micah 7:17 (in simile; see also Gen 3:14 ). d. as crafty tempter Gen 3:1-2 , 4 , 13 , 14 . 2 ׳נ (הַ)נְּחשֶׁת , bronze image of serpent Num 21:9 (twice in verse); 2Kin 18:4 (compare נְחֻשְׁתָּן ). 3 mythological ׳נ בָּרִחַ Job 26:13 fleeing serpent , of eclipse-dragon (compare לִנְיָתָן 3:6 ); also נ ׳לִוְיָתָן עֲקַלָּתוֺן נ ׳לִוְיָתָן ֗֗֗ בּרִחַ Isa 27:1 (symbolic of world-powers); ׳נ of sea-monster Amos 9:3 . &#8212; ׳נ with verb נָשַׁךְ bite Num 21:6 8 t. On supernatural character of serpents in Arabic belief see Nö Zeitschr. Für Völkerpsychol. i.(1860), 412-416 RS Kinship 197, Semitic i. 421 f. , 2d ed, 442 We Skizzen iii.147, Arab. Heid. 2, 152 f. Jacob Arab. Dicht. iv. 5","rootNote":"from 5172 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Kgs 18 4","keyReferences":["2Kgs 18 4","Amos 5 19","Amos 9 3","Deut 8 15","Eccl 10 8","Eccl 10 11","Exod 4 3","Exod 7 15"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":31,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Kgs 18 4","book":"2Kgs","chapter":18,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נְחַ֨שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"Amos 5 19","book":"Amos","chapter":5,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/נָּחָֽשׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Amos 9 3","book":"Amos","chapter":9,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/נָּחָ֖שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 8 15","book":"Deut","chapter":8,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָחָ֤שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"Eccl 10 8","book":"Eccl","chapter":10,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָחָֽשׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"Eccl 10 11","book":"Eccl","chapter":10,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/נָּחָ֖שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"referen